// Change: new rule
// Title: HackTool - PKINITtools Execution
// Sigma ID: 04b81869-15dd-47ce-afbb-d07707141ba0
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-04-21 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1649, T1558
// Description: Detects execution of PKINITtools scripts (gettgtpkinit.py, getnthash.py, gets4uticket.py) used
//   to obtain Kerberos TGTs via PKINIT authentication and recover NT hashes through the UnPAC-the-
//   Hash technique after obtaining an Active Directory certificate.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/dirkjanm/PKINITtools
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/6b9ade7935a13d35a57e75ff2587fbedcc53ef56/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_pkinittools.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\python" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName contains "python") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "gettgtpkinit.py" or ProcessCommandLine contains "getnthash.py" or ProcessCommandLine contains "gets4uticket.py")
